{"name":"Celery Root","hex":"#d4e4ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"celery root","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of celeriac."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/celery_root"}],"entries":[{"title":"Celeriac","blocks":[{"text":"Celeriac, also called celery root, knob celery, and turnip-rooted celery, is a group of cultivars of Apium graveolens cultivated for their edible bulb-like hypocotyl, and shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/C%C3%A9leri-rave-fendu.jpg/330px-C%C3%A9leri-rave-fendu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeriac","wikidata":"Q575174"},{"title":"Celery","blocks":[{"text":"Celery is a cultivated plant belonging to the species Apium graveolens in the family Apiaceae that has been used as a vegetable since ancient times."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Celery_1.jpg/330px-Celery_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celery","wikidata":"Q23012379"},{"title":"Root","blocks":[{"text":"In vascular plants, the roots are the organs of a plant that are modified to provide anchorage for the plant and take in water and nutrients into the plant body, which allows plants to grow taller and faster. They are most often below the surface of the soil, but roots can also be aerial or aerating, that is, growing up above the ground or especially above water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg/330px-Primary_and_secondary_cotton_roots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Root","wikidata":"Q41500"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Tselina.png/330px-Tselina.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa